./analysis/s17-claude-b-api-native-flow.json:114:      "evidence": "P has stronger external/local verification for 'an accessible electronic JPEG source exists' (real binary symbols + independent third-party functional report) than E's longer internal inference chains (open blockers in RESEARCH_TASKS.md sessions 13-16: topology 0x2a creator, YC format, CBID_ENCODE_STILL release timing). P has weaker support for the mission-specific question 'S2 triggers electronic capture': no evidence ties the physical button to CameraSequence in Sony's stock firmware or in any known third-party app; the only real code (PMCADemo) wires the button to conventional takePicture(). No code-level link found between CameraSequence/ScalarDaemon and ObjCamera/ObjEffect/PbCap (architecture E's object family); a shared-backend relationship with architecture B/F (SFRA/DMM, also served by ScalarDaemon) is more plausible but unverified (same daemon class family, no traced call graph).",
./analysis/s17-claude-b-api-native-flow.json-115-      "notes": "EXPLICIT: does not declare that electronic capture via S2 works. CameraSequence is real and verified; its connection to the physical shutter button is unverified and would require new application-level integration work."
